    "answer": {
      "short": "$324,\\ 720,\\ 828$.",
      "worked": "Divisibility by 4 requires the last two digits to be $20$, $24$ or $28$. Let $a$ be the hundreds digit, with $1\\le a\\le9$.\n\nFor an ending of $20$, the digit sum is $a+2$, so $a=7$ and the number is $720$.\n\nFor an ending of $24$, the digit sum is $a+6$, so $a=3$ and the number is $324$.\n\nFor an ending of $28$, the digit sum is $a+10$, so $a=8$ and the number is $828$.\n\nThus all such numbers are $324$, $720$ and $828$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 52
